---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: Neighbourhood webring
eyebrow: Member list / reshuffled each build
description: A hand-made path through sites belonging to meetup neighbours and open-web friends.
permalink: /webring/
---
<div class="ring-howto">
  <div>
    <p class="kicker">Link to your next neighbour</p>
    <code>{{ site.url }}/webring/&lt;your-slug&gt;/next/</code>
  </div>
  <div>
    <p class="kicker">Link to your previous neighbour</p>
    <code>{{ site.url }}/webring/&lt;your-slug&gt;/previous/</code>
  </div>
</div>

<ol class="ring-list">
  {% for member in webring.members %}
    <li>
      <div>
        <h2><a href="{{ member.url }}">{{ member.title }}</a></h2>
        <p>{{ member.description }}</p>
        <p class="slug">slug: <strong>{{ member.slug }}</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="ring-list__links">
        <a class="button" href="/webring/{{ member.slug }}/previous/" aria-label="Previous site from {{ member.title }}">← prev</a>
        <a class="button button--signal" href="/webring/{{ member.slug }}/next/" aria-label="Next site from {{ member.title }}">next →</a>
      </div>
    </li>
  {% endfor %}
</ol>

{% note "Build-time shuffle" %}
The member data is shuffled once during each Eleventy build. Every <code>next</code> and <code>previous</code> page in that deployment uses the same order, including wrap-around at both ends. Updating the site creates a new route around the ring—no function, database or server process required.
{% endnote %}
